          "title": "14. Corrosion of metals",
          "text": "Corrosion is the deterioration of a metal through reaction with its environment. Iron rusts in the presence of both oxygen and water, forming hydrated iron(III) oxide. Aluminium behaves differently because its oxide layer is compact and protective. Corrosion can be controlled by painting, oiling, galvanising, electroplating, alloying and other surface-protection methods. The best method depends on the metal and the service environment."
